<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states the PDE, the 24.08 µm peak condition, and the predecessor anisotropy. Lean theorems check the integer Turing margins for both axes and both species. The Lean integers are rounded to 0.01, and gamma's calibration is described in prose rather than derived in a cited equation number from Nakamasu 2009." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "sigma_mode is the larger eigenvalue of gamma*J - k^2 D for the Schnakenberg Jacobian, and integrate steps that operator with spectral diffusion. Anisotropy keeps Dv_y on the calibrated peak and lowers Dv_x. gamma is a scale calibration, not a number copied from Nakamasu et al. 2009." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "PDE growth versus analytical sigma(k) has Pearson r = 0.9975 and RMSE = 0.0192. The rendered-GIF coherency (0.4399) is not the specimen coherency (0.3887). The predecessor wavelength on the dedicated run is 20.64 µm against the rerio 24.08 µm target. The KS sample has only 12 points, so D = 0.25 sits on the reference ceiling and is a weak goodness-of-fit statement." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-curve-pearson-r-of-pde-growth-versus-analytical-sigma-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse-between-analytical-and-numerical-growth-rates>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-negative-control-field-amplitude>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-kolmogorov-smirnov-statistic-of-analytical-versus-numerical-growth-rate-samples>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-predecessor-danio-nigrofasciatus-dominant-wavelength-at-anisotropy-1-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-segmented-specimen-foreground-fraction-versus-gif-occupancy>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-selected-dorsoventral-wavelength-of-the-holocene-danio-rerio-field>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-structure-tensor-coherency-of-the-rendered-gif>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 83.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates an anisotropic Schnakenberg system whose dorsoventral dispersion peak sits on k_c = 2π/24.08 µm. Inhibitor anisotropy 3.85 (extant D. rerio, 0 Ma) produces horizontal stripes; anisotropy 1.12 (predecessor D. nigrofasciatus, same cellular scale) does not. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9975, RMSE = 0.0192, selected wavelength = 24.08 µm on three noise seeds. The GIF is a 12-frame, 960×540 magnification of the 144.48 µm window inside the segmented specimen outline (CV similarity 74.5). The rendered stripes are still a gray sinusoid, and the comparison figure does not show that composite. Overall 83.7/100 (faithfulness 82.0, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 469820 B, 1488×1032 px, artifact_sha256 bce4762d3451a3910ffd3cbe0f23b28ea3485f00360100014b31e51e0c1fad6f (sha256 bce4762d3451a3910ffd3cbe0f23b28ea3485f00360100014b31e51e0c1fad6f), spec_fingerprint d7d1a6ee4915a8532ac3ba145d5dd7b6436e0f7006bd83ec8bd0ab39b939e0f7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d7d1a6ee4915a8532ac3ba145d5dd7b6436e0f7006bd83ec8bd0ab39b939e0f7; artifact_sha256: bce4762d3451a3910ffd3cbe0f23b28ea3485f00360100014b31e51e0c1fad6f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=dbe49b6901b94381..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_rerio_specimen.jpg=850b2d4a94c7cbcb..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=8456a78d5a6e1822..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=e77f417b131e9ec8..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=7dfbf8b27236cb36...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a two-species reaction-diffusion system has a critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: zebrafish melanophores and xanthophores interact as a short-range activation / long-range inhibition pair. | Hiscock & Megason 2015: anisotropy can restrict the unstable wavevector to one axis and thereby orient stripes. | Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: D. nigrofasciatus expresses broken stripes or spots relative to D. rerio.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics with a=0.11, b=1.24, Du=0.80, Dv_y=20.80, gamma=0.1989, anisotropy 3.85, on a 288.96 × 144.48 µm periodic window. | Numerical growth rates compared with the analytical eigenvalue on 12 wavenumbers. | Fish outline segmented from the vendored specimen and used as the GIF domain.; transfer_boundary: The 24.08 µm window is magnified onto the adult outline. Adult flank stripes are not 24 µm wide. | gamma and Dv_y are chosen so the dispersion peak lies on the assigned scale; they are not a published parameter table.; does_not_claim: That this continuum field is the Nakamasu three-cell network or a Volkening-Sandstede agent model. | That D. nigrofasciatus was measured at 24.08 µm in the cited papers; the predecessor contrast is the anisotropy mechanism at this assigned scale. | A nanopublication signature. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is not present.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: A second assessor on a different model has not scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: Recompute the Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic on a finer wavenumber grid so D is not forced onto 0.25 by a 12-point sample.",
        "remediation needed: Render the comparison PNG with the fish-mask composite beside the photograph, and sharpen the GIF pigment so stripes use the specimen dark and light palette instead of a gray sinusoid.",
        "remediation needed: gamma = 0.1989 is a scale calibration to 24.08 µm, not a value transcribed from a published table." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.37e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The anisotropy sweep 1.12, 2.0, 3.85, 6.0 raises gradient anisotropy from 1.20 to 6.00 monotonically, and the equal-diffusion control collapses to amplitude ~1e-11. The predecessor regime is the low end of the same sweep." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

