<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) (Danio rerio)",
        "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 1) faithfully reproduces Danio rerio morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Danio rerio" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A nanopublication signature. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is not present.",
        "does_not_claim: That D. nigrofasciatus was measured at 24.08 µm in the cited papers; the predecessor contrast is the anisotropy mechanism at this assigned scale.",
        "does_not_claim: That this continuum field is the Nakamasu three-cell network or a Volkening-Sandstede agent model.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fish outline segmented from the vendored specimen and used as the GIF domain.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Numerical growth rates compared with the analytical eigenvalue on 12 wavenumbers.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics with a=0.11, b=1.24, Du=0.80, Dv_y=20.80, gamma=0.1989, anisotropy 3.85, on a 288.96 × 144.48 µm periodic window.",
        "reported_in_source: Hiscock & Megason 2015: anisotropy can restrict the unstable wavevector to one axis and thereby orient stripes.",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. 2009: zebrafish melanophores and xanthophores interact as a short-range activation / long-range inhibition pair.",
        "reported_in_source: Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: D. nigrofasciatus expresses broken stripes or spots relative to D. rerio.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a two-species reaction-diffusion system has a critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 24.08 µm window is magnified onto the adult outline. Adult flank stripes are not 24 µm wide.",
        "transfer_boundary: gamma and Dv_y are chosen so the dispersion peak lies on the assigned scale; they are not a published parameter table." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Danio rerio" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; output: docs/media/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a two-species reaction-diffusion system has a critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: zebrafish melanophores and xanthophores interact as a short-range activation / long-range inhibition pair. | Hiscock & Megason 2015: anisotropy can restrict the unstable wavevector to one axis and thereby orient stripes. | Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: D. nigrofasciatus expresses broken stripes or spots relative to D. rerio.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics with a=0.11, b=1.24, Du=0.80, Dv_y=20.80, gamma=0.1989, anisotropy 3.85, on a 288.96 × 144.48 µm periodic window. | Numerical growth rates compared with the analytical eigenvalue on 12 wavenumbers. | Fish outline segmented from the vendored specimen and used as the GIF domain.; transfer_boundary: The 24.08 µm window is magnified onto the adult outline. Adult flank stripes are not 24 µm wide. | gamma and Dv_y are chosen so the dispersion peak lies on the assigned scale; they are not a published parameter table.; does_not_claim: That this continuum field is the Nakamasu three-cell network or a Volkening-Sandstede agent model. | That D. nigrofasciatus was measured at 24.08 µm in the cited papers; the predecessor contrast is the anisotropy mechanism at this assigned scale. | A nanopublication signature. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is not present.]; phenomenon_size: 20 µm (2.018e-05 m, log10=-4.695 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 20 µm to 4.5 cm): 20 µm:danio-aesculapii-bioelectric-polarity, 63 µm:danio-aesculapii-vertex-packing, 1.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength, 2.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-clock-wavefront, 4.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-morphogen-condensation, 5.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-elastic-buckling, 6.3 mm:danio-aesculapii-flux-canalization, 8.8 mm:danio-aesculapii-branching-tree" ;
